  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;WILLY SCHWABACHER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Willy Schwabacher is a German numismatist known for his contributions to the field of numismatics and his academic background at the Technical University of Darmstadt."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0198</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNIVERSITY OF NOTTINGHAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"University of Nottingham is where Willy Schwabacher spent his undergraduate years, surrounded by historic architecture and a vibrant cultural scene."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0198</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GEORGE GREEN LIBRARY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"George Green Library is a library at the University of Nottingham where Willy Schwabacher spent time researching."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0198</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DR. EMILIA FOTHERGILL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dr. Emilia Fothergill is a little-known scholar who wrote an obscure treatise on medieval coinage, captivating Willy Schwabacher with her writing style."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0198</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEPARTMENT OF ARCHAEOLOGY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Department of Archaeology at the University of Nottingham is where Willy Schwabacher met Dr. Fothergill."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0198</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF DARMSTADT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Technical University of Darmstadt is a German institution where Willy Schwabacher pursued his education in the early 20th century."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0198</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HOLY ROMAN EMPIRE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Holy Roman Empire is the subject of Willy Schwabacher's research on coinage."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0198</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CRUSADES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Crusades are discussed in the context of Dr. Fothergill's lecture and Willy Schwabacher's research interests."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0198</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NUMISMATICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Numismatics is Schwabacher's area of expertise, requiring knowledge of metallurgy, materials science, and historical context."&lt;SEP&gt;"Numismatics is the field of study that Willy Schwabacher specializes in, involving the collection and study of coins and medals."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0198</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNIVERSITY OF DARMSTADT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"University of Darmstadt is a German institution where Willy Schwabacher pursued his education in the early 20th century."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0198</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GERMANY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Germany is the country where Willy Schwabacher grew up and attended university."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0198</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GRAND DUKE LUDWIG IV OF HESSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Grand Duke Ludwig IV of Hesse founded the Technical University of Darmstadt in 1877."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0198</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METALLURGY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FIELD"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Metallurgy is a key component of Schwabacher's numismatic research, essential for understanding coin composition."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metallurgy is an important aspect of Willy Schwabacher's numismatic research, especially in relation to coinage."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0198</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MATERIALS SCIENCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FIELD"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Materials Science is a key component of Schwabacher's numismatic research, essential for understanding coin composition and properties."&lt;SEP&gt;"Materials science is another important aspect of Willy Schwabacher's numismatic research, especially in relation to coinage."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0198</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HISTORICAL CONTEXT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FIELD"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Historical Context is a key component of Schwabacher's numismatic research, essential for understanding the cultural and temporal significance of coins."&lt;SEP&gt;"Historical context is crucial for Willy Schwabacher's numismatic research, especially in understanding the background of coinage."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0198</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTELLECTUAL CURIOSITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Intellectual curiosity is a quality instilled in Willy Schwabacher by his education at the Technical University of Darmstadt."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0198</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CREATIVITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Creativity is a quality instilled in Willy Schwabacher by his education at the Technical University of Darmstadt."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0198</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACADEMIC COMMUNITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Academic community is a network Willy Schwabacher aspires to join through his research and connections."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0198</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SCHWABACHER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Schwabacher is a researcher with a background in natural sciences, chemistry, physics, mathematics, and numismatics, known for his meticulous attention to detail."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0198</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNIVERSITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The University emphasizes experimentation and hands-on learning, providing a solid foundation for Schwabacher's future work in numismatics."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0198</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHEMISTRY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"SUBJECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chemistry is part of Schwabacher's coursework, contributing to his foundational knowledge."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0198</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHYSICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"SUBJECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Physics is part of Schwabacher's coursework, contributing to his foundational knowledge."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0198</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MATHEMATICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"SUBJECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mathematics is part of Schwabacher's coursework, contributing to his foundational knowledge."</data>
